type: web_research
title: "Claude Code Hooks API: Return Values, Exit Codes, and Decision Control"
key_insights[8]: Exit code 0 = success; exit code 2 = blocking error; any other code = non-blocking error,"PreToolUse uses hookSpecificOutput with permissionDecision (allow/deny/ask), NOT top-level decision field","PermissionRequest uses hookSpecificOutput.decision.behavior (allow/deny), can also modify updatedInput",JSON output ONLY processed on exit 0; exit 2 ignores JSON and uses stderr as error message,"When PreToolUse hook errors or crashes: no documentation on default behavior—behavior appears event-specific with bugs",No built-in 'force approval' mechanism; approval patterns cannot be skipped once previously allowed,"Three hook types: command (shell script), prompt (single LLM turn), agent (multi-turn with tools)","Prompt hooks default to Haiku model, agent hooks spawn full subagent with 60s timeout default"
refs[5]: "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks - Official comprehensive reference","https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/24327 - PreToolUse exit code 2 causes stop","https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/13744 - PreToolUse exit code 2 doesn't block Write/Edit","https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/26923 - PreToolUse exit code 2 doesn't block Task","https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/19298 - PermissionRequest hook decision ignored"
recommendations[6]: Use exit 0 + JSON with hookSpecificOutput for rich control; exit 2 + stderr for simple blocking,Test PreToolUse hooks thoroughly—GitHub issues show blocking failures on Write/Edit/Task tools,"PermissionRequest has known race condition: ~1-2s timeout means dialog may appear despite hook returning allow","For 'always require approval': use permissionDecision ask in PreToolUse, cannot force past prior allow",SessionStart hook can set CLAUDE_ENV_FILE to persist environment variables for all Bash commands,"Async hooks (async: true) cannot block or control behavior—only for side effects like logging/testing"
